And then, on Monday --
Voting ends Sunday night,

00:00:38.438 --> 00:00:39.806 line:0%
so Monday,
we'll decide which one

00:00:39.806 --> 00:00:41.207 line:0%
we're all going to
read together.

00:00:41.207 --> 00:00:42.208 line:0%
-Aww.

00:00:42.208 --> 00:00:43.376 line:0%
-Yeah.
And then we'll read books.

00:00:43.376 --> 00:00:44.910
We'll talk about it.

00:00:44.910 --> 00:00:46.278
It's like a summer read.

00:00:46.278 --> 00:00:47.380
-Yeah.
-This is what you need.

00:00:47.380 --> 00:00:50.149
Yeah. So, here we go.
Here's the books.

00:00:50.149 --> 00:00:52.652
I'll go through the plots fast.

00:00:52.652 --> 00:00:55.388
Emily Henry,
"People We Meet on Vacation."

00:00:55.388 --> 00:00:59.091
Basically, a guy and girl go on
vacation together for years.

00:00:59.091 --> 00:01:01.126
Then they have a fallout.
They don't go one year.

00:01:01.126 --> 00:01:04.264
Then they decide to go back and
go on vacation and just, like,

00:01:04.264 --> 00:01:05.364
fix the problems they have.

00:01:05.364 --> 00:01:06.633
But they ask the question,

00:01:06.633 --> 00:01:08.868
can men and women
actually be "just friends"?

00:01:08.868 --> 00:01:11.037
-Ooh!

00:01:11.037 --> 00:01:12.272
Ooh!
-What?!

00:01:12.272 --> 00:01:13.840
-Snap!

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:17.977
-"Razorblade Tears."
Yeah, this is by S.A. Cosby.

00:01:17.977 --> 00:01:20.179
His last novel won
an "L.A. Times" book award

00:01:20.179 --> 00:01:21.213
for Best Mystery.

00:01:21.213 --> 00:01:22.548
He knows how to do it.

00:01:22.548 --> 00:01:26.619
Basically, these two ex-cons --
their sons are murdered,

00:01:26.619 --> 00:01:28.721
but the local cops
won't do anything about it.

00:01:28.721 --> 00:01:31.690
So they take matters
into their own hands.

00:01:31.690 --> 00:01:35.628
There's twists.
There's turns.

00:01:35.628 --> 00:01:36.796
"One Last Stop."

00:01:36.796 --> 00:01:40.333
This is a, like,
a magic type of romance book.

00:01:40.333 --> 00:01:41.967
"New York Times"
best-selling author.

00:01:41.967 --> 00:01:43.869
A girl gives up on love.

00:01:43.869 --> 00:01:46.306
She's like, "Eh, forget it."
She's in New York.

00:01:46.306 --> 00:01:48.540
Goes on the subway and meets
this beautiful girl,

00:01:48.540 --> 00:01:49.709
and they fall in love,

00:01:49.709 --> 00:01:52.178
but the girl is trapped in
1970-something.

00:01:52.178 --> 00:01:54.146
-Ooh!
-It's a time thing.

00:01:54.146 --> 00:01:56.182
Yeah, it's awesome.
Will she find love?

00:01:56.182 --> 00:01:59.251
Will she get to her stop?
I don't know.

00:01:59.251 --> 00:02:01.453
-Just one last one.

00:02:01.453 --> 00:02:03.489
-This is "Crying in H Mart,"
Michelle Zauner.

00:02:03.489 --> 00:02:06.425
[ Crowd cheers ]
I know -- I love H Mart.

00:02:06.425 --> 00:02:09.595
And -- But you know her as
Japanese Breakfast.

00:02:09.595 --> 00:02:11.864
This is Japanese Breakfast.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:11.864 --> 00:02:13.265
So this is a memoir.

00:02:13.265 --> 00:02:15.168
And it's beautiful.

00:02:15.168 --> 00:02:17.069
It's about growing up
Asian-American

00:02:17.069 --> 00:02:18.404
in the United States.

00:02:18.404 --> 00:02:21.174
And her mom would always teach
her about Korean culture.

00:02:21.174 --> 00:02:23.109
And then,
after her mom passes away,

00:02:23.109 --> 00:02:25.478
how the things
her mom taught her

00:02:25.478 --> 00:02:26.912
helped her shape
who she is today.

00:02:26.912 --> 00:02:29.315
-Aww.
-It's cool.

00:02:29.315 --> 00:02:32.551
This is "The Final Revival
of Opal &amp; Nev,"

00:02:32.551 --> 00:02:34.220
by Dawnie Walton.

00:02:34.220 --> 00:02:35.688
Debut novel.

00:02:35.688 --> 00:02:38.824
Debut author here, so if you
want to support a debut author.

00:02:38.824 --> 00:02:40.226
"New York Times" calls it

00:02:40.226 --> 00:02:43.896
"A packed time capsule that
doubles as a stick of dynamite."

00:02:43.896 --> 00:02:46.131
-Whoa! Don't let that blow up.

00:02:46.131 --> 00:02:47.133
-I didn't even have to tell you
what the story is about.

00:02:47.133 --> 00:02:48.467
-Yeah.

00:02:48.467 --> 00:02:53.973
-But it's a group from
the '70s that want to reunite,

00:02:53.973 --> 00:02:56.543
but then some
dark secret comes up,

00:02:56.543 --> 00:02:59.578
and they're like,
"Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa."

00:02:59.578 --> 00:03:02.114
Then this one here, "The Plot."

00:03:02.114 --> 00:03:05.685
This is by Jean Hanff Korelitz.

00:03:05.685 --> 00:03:07.754
This is the author of the book
that "The Undoing" was based on.

00:03:07.754 --> 00:03:09.087
-Ooh!

00:03:09.087 --> 00:03:10.356
-Yeah, it's the new book.

00:03:10.356 --> 00:03:13.525
And here's the plot of
"The Plot."

00:03:13.525 --> 00:03:15.794
An English teacher is teaching
a class on how to write a book.

00:03:15.794 --> 00:03:18.464
One student has a good story,
but the student dies.

00:03:18.464 --> 00:03:21.066
-Ooh!
-So what does the teacher do?

00:03:21.066 --> 00:03:22.968
Takes the story.
-Ooh!

00:03:22.968 --> 00:03:26.172
-And he becomes the
famous author from the story.

00:03:26.172 --> 00:03:27.673
Until one day,
he gets an e-mail.

00:03:27.673 --> 00:03:29.776
Guess what the subject says.
-Say what?

00:03:29.776 --> 00:03:32.812
-"You are a thief."
-Ooh!

00:03:32.812 --> 00:03:35.147
Dang!

00:03:35.147 --> 00:03:37.850
-So, what I was thinking was --
-Plot of "The Plot."

00:03:37.850 --> 00:03:40.019
Real quick, so before -- 'Cause
you got to get your votes in.

00:03:40.019 --> 00:03:41.888
These are all winners,
to be honest,

00:03:41.888 --> 00:03:43.323
so support all of them.

00:03:43.323 --> 00:03:46.225
Go to your local bookstore,
get all of them, if you want.

00:03:46.225 --> 00:03:47.460
That's really all we care about.

00:03:47.460 --> 00:03:50.029 line:0%
We want everyone to win here.

00:03:50.029 --> 00:03:52.932 line:0%
But I want one to be chosen

00:03:52.932 --> 00:03:54.566 line:0%
